29
00:01:49,520 --> 00:01:50,630
And.

30
00:01:51,800 --> 00:01:52,850
Next one.

31
00:01:54,860 --> 00:01:56,150
Say the words.

32
00:02:00,410 --> 00:02:01,500
Okay, let's check.

33
00:02:01,520 --> 00:02:03,980
She studied French.

34
00:02:04,010 --> 00:02:07,070
She didn't study French.

35
00:02:07,070 --> 00:02:10,040
And did she study French?

36
00:02:10,070 --> 00:02:13,610
I hope you said those words, guys.

37
00:02:13,730 --> 00:02:19,130
So now our job is to learn a sentence in present into past.

38
00:02:19,160 --> 00:02:23,600
So here we have sentences in present simple.

39
00:02:23,870 --> 00:02:25,160
We use present simple.

40
00:02:25,160 --> 00:02:27,740
When we say about things we do sometimes.

41
00:02:27,740 --> 00:02:30,200
Often all the time, from time to time.

42
00:02:30,200 --> 00:02:33,080
And we need to turn them into past.

43
00:02:33,080 --> 00:02:41,030
And we use to pass when we want to talk about something in the past, like yesterday, last year, a

44
00:02:41,030 --> 00:02:42,560
month ago, and so on.

45
00:02:42,710 --> 00:02:43,310
Okay.

46
00:02:43,340 --> 00:02:44,180
Our sentence.

47
00:02:44,180 --> 00:02:45,500
I am a car.

48
00:02:46,770 --> 00:02:50,900
How should we turn it into past?

49
00:02:50,910 --> 00:02:51,320
Simple.

50
00:02:51,330 --> 00:02:53,790
For example, yesterday I.

51
00:02:53,820 --> 00:02:58,350
So we need to take M and use the past form of it.

52
00:02:58,380 --> 00:03:06,810
I am I was I was AQI two years ago last year and so on.

53
00:03:07,380 --> 00:03:07,770
Okay.

54
00:03:07,800 --> 00:03:10,050
Second sentence.

55
