I write code.

56
00:03:12,060 --> 00:03:15,960
So write it's irregular verb.

57
00:03:15,960 --> 00:03:23,490
So we need to check the table of irregular verbs to find the past simple form of write.

58
00:03:24,120 --> 00:03:26,490
So it should be.

59
00:03:26,520 --> 00:03:30,150
I write road code.

60
00:03:30,600 --> 00:03:31,410
Good.

61
00:03:32,130 --> 00:03:33,270
Next question.

62
00:03:33,450 --> 00:03:43,710
So the sentence I read the requirements often from time to time and in the past we say.

63
00:03:44,550 --> 00:03:45,570
Can you help me?

64
00:03:46,080 --> 00:03:48,420
I so read.

65
00:03:48,450 --> 00:03:51,060
Is it regular or irregular?

66
00:03:51,450 --> 00:03:53,100
It's irregular.

67
00:03:53,130 --> 00:03:53,790
Read.

68
00:03:53,790 --> 00:03:54,550
Read.

69
00:03:54,630 --> 00:03:56,790
But tricky thing.

70
00:03:57,750 --> 00:03:59,400
It is spelled the same.

71
00:03:59,730 --> 00:04:02,100
So you just read it?

72
00:04:02,810 --> 00:04:04,610
In a different way.

73
00:04:04,850 --> 00:04:14,210
I read the requirements yesterday, last Tuesday, a few years ago, and so on.

74
00:04:15,120 --> 00:04:15,810
All right.

75
00:04:15,810 --> 00:04:18,570
So we need to make it look good.

76
00:04:20,510 --> 00:04:22,250
Okay, here we go.

77
00:04:22,250 --> 00:04:26,080
We already have three sentences in the past.

78
00:04:26,370 --> 00:04:27,470
Looks nice.

79
00:04:27,800 --> 00:04:29,300
Okay, next one.

80
00:04:29,300 --> 00:04:32,330
She writes test cases.

81
00:04:32,330 --> 00:04:34,280
She writes test cases.

82
00:04:34,280 --> 00:04:40,310
And in the past, we already know that to write is irregular.

83
00:04:40,610 --> 00:04:48,170
She wrote test cases, as you can see for present.

84
00:04:48,170 --> 00:04:48,890
Simple.

85
00:04:49,980 --> 00:04:50,640
We?

86
00:04:50,940 --> 00:04:51,810
Sorry.

87
00:04:52,290 --> 00:04:53,100
Yes.

88
00:04:53,250 --> 00:04:54,480
Like that for present.

89
00:04:54,480 --> 00:04:55,050
Simple.

90
00:04:55,050 --> 00:04:58,800
We add as because we have she third person.

91
00:04:58,800 --> 00:04:59,730
She writes.

92
00:04:59,730 --> 00:05:04,980
He writes But for past simple we don't need to add anything.

93
00:05:04,980 --> 00:05:07,170
So I wrote code.

94
00:05:07,170 --> 00:05:09,120
She wrote test cases.

95
00:05:09,120 --> 00:05:10,410
It is the same.

96
00:05:10,650 --> 00:05:13,860
And we have zoom meetings.

97
00:05:14,640 --> 00:05:16,560
How to make it in past.

98
00:05:16,560 --> 00:05:17,220
Simple.

99
00:05:17,640 --> 00:05:18,420
We.

100
00:05:20,180 --> 00:05:25,100
So half is also irregular and it's had in the past.

101
00:05:25,130 --> 00:05:26,960
We had Zoom.

102
00:05:27,790 --> 00:05:28,870
Meetings.

103
00:05:30,370 --> 00:05:35,620
So those are our sentences in the past.

104
00:05:36,130 --> 00:05:37,900
Okay, cool.

105
00:05:38,110 --> 00:05:39,340
Let's move on.

106
00:05:40,330 --> 00:05:43,580
We will practice making questions.

107
00:05:43,600 --> 00:05:45,400
We have this sentence.

108
00:05:45,610 --> 00:05:49,900
I worked at IBM in 2009.

109
00:05:50,700 --> 00:05:55,050
Easy right sentence in the past about some past experience.

110
00:05:55,500 --> 00:05:59,670
Now you can see that I underlined some words.

111
00:05:59,700 --> 00:06:04,390
I worked at IBM 2009.

112
00:06:04,410 --> 00:06:14,190
So our job is we have to make a question for each underlined word.

113
00:06:14,340 --> 00:06:19,380
Okay, let's start and you will see how we do it.

114
00:06:19,890 --> 00:06:24,530
I worked at IBM in 2009, so let's start with this.

115
00:06:24,540 --> 00:06:30,620
So we have to make a question for the word I.

116
00:06:31,470 --> 00:06:33,420
So I is a person.

117
00:06:33,420 --> 00:06:36,690
So we start the question with who?

118
00:06:36,720 --> 00:06:40,890
Who worked at IBM.

119
00:06:42,060 --> 00:06:42,810
In.

120
00:06:44,380 --> 00:06:47,290
In 2009.

121
00:06:47,320 --> 00:06:50,380
So that is our first question.

122
00:06:50,590 --> 00:06:54,220
Who worked at IBM in 2009?

123
00:06:54,430 --> 00:06:59,500
I worked at IBM in 2009.

124
00:07:00,190 --> 00:07:00,880
Good.

125
00:07:00,910 --> 00:07:06,430
Now we need to make a question for the word worked.

126
00:07:07,410 --> 00:07:10,200
What question can we make?

127
00:07:10,590 --> 00:07:11,820
We can say.

128
00:07:17,100 --> 00:07:18,210
What?

129
00:07:19,280 --> 00:07:20,510
We need auxiliary.

130
00:07:21,460 --> 00:07:22,240
Did.

131
00:07:23,500 --> 00:07:26,920
I do at.

132
00:07:27,680 --> 00:07:31,430
IBM in 2009.

133
00:07:32,860 --> 00:07:34,990
So that is our second.

134
00:07:35,730 --> 00:07:36,600
Question.

135
00:07:38,710 --> 00:07:43,140
What did I do at IBM in 2009?

136
00:07:43,150 --> 00:07:51,580
So here we introduce an auxiliary did what did I do?

137
00:07:52,810 --> 00:07:58,150
All right, now we need to ask a question for IBM.

138
00:07:58,720 --> 00:08:10,630
So IBM is a company, so it's a place so we can start our question with where.

139
00:08:12,370 --> 00:08:18,080
Did I work in 2009?

140
00:08:18,100 --> 00:08:20,910
Where did I work in 2009?

141
00:08:20,920 --> 00:08:24,730
I worked at IBM in 2009.

142
00:08:24,730 --> 00:08:27,490
So again, we see that here.

143
00:08:27,490 --> 00:08:33,040
We have worked in the past and here we have just work infinitive.

144
00:08:33,040 --> 00:08:39,550
So if we have auxiliary did, where did we don't need?

145
00:08:40,900 --> 00:08:41,650
The ending.

146
00:08:41,680 --> 00:08:42,490
Ed here.

147
00:08:42,490 --> 00:08:43,810
Where did I work?

148
00:08:43,810 --> 00:08:45,220
Where did I study?

149
00:08:45,250 --> 00:08:47,680
Where did he learn Python?

150
00:08:48,190 --> 00:08:48,850
Okay.

151
00:08:48,850 --> 00:08:51,490
And the last word is.

152
00:08:55,100 --> 00:08:56,000
2009.

153
00:08:56,000 --> 00:08:58,430
So it's about time.

154
00:08:59,340 --> 00:09:03,480
So we can start the question with one.

155
00:09:05,440 --> 00:09:06,040
Did.

156
00:09:07,230 --> 00:09:09,500
I work in Toyota.

157
00:09:09,750 --> 00:09:10,470
Oh, sorry.

158
00:09:10,470 --> 00:09:11,550
When did I work?

159
00:09:12,060 --> 00:09:13,110
No.

160
00:09:14,030 --> 00:09:15,060
At IBM?

161
00:09:15,080 --> 00:09:15,680
Yeah.

162
00:09:16,310 --> 00:09:19,700
When did I work at IBM?

163
00:09:20,630 --> 00:09:25,130
I worked at IBM in 2009.

164
00:09:25,550 --> 00:09:26,390
Okay.

165
00:09:26,420 --> 00:09:28,900
Take a look at our questions.

166
00:09:29,290 --> 00:09:33,740
Also, I worked at IBM in 2009.

167
00:09:33,740 --> 00:09:36,170
You can ask one more question.

168
00:09:37,100 --> 00:09:41,320
Did I work at IBM in 2009?

169
00:09:41,330 --> 00:09:47,060
Yes, I worked at IBM in 2009.

170
00:09:47,570 --> 00:09:56,000
Okay, guys, I hope that that would help you to make questions, to ask questions, and see you next

171
00:09:56,000 --> 00:09:56,510
time.

172
00:09:56,780 --> 00:09:57,530
Bye.
